exec
Usage: exec [COMMAND [ARG]...]

Shell builtin. Replace the shell process with COMMAND -- same PID, no
fork, no return. With no command, apply its redirections to the current
shell instead.

vos's init ends with `exec /bin/sh`, so the shell becomes PID 1 rather
than a child of it.

	exec 3<&0	open fd 3 as a copy of stdin

See also: eval, exit
